    "https://jobs.du.edu/jobs/executive-assistant-and-office-operations-manager-office-of-the-general-counsel-denver-co-colorado-united-states": {
      "title": "Executive Assistant and Office Operations Manager, Office of The General Counsel",
      "description": "Executive Assistant and Office Operations Manager, Office of The General Counsel - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Executive Assistant and Office Operations Manager, Office of The General Counsel 499124 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Full-Time Closing on: Nov 9 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Office of the General Counsel provides legal advice and counsel to the University of Denver on a broad range of matters arising from the University's operations, including contract review, litigation management, regulatory compliance, risk management, employment matters, governance, academic affairs, athletics, student affairs, and other legal issues affecting the institution. Position Summary The Executive Assistant and Office Manager serves as the senior administrative and operational support professional for the Office of the General Counsel (“OGC”). This position provides executive-level support to the Senior Vice Chancellor for Legal Affairs and General Counsel, administrative support to all attorneys within OGC, and management of the administrative and operational functions of the office. This individual regularly works with highly sensitive and confidential information and must exercise exceptional judgment, discretion, professionalism, and independent decision-making. This individual also serves as an ambassador for OGC to internal and external parties, creating a welcoming and professional environment in the office. This position reports directly to the Senior Vice Chancellor for Legal Affairs and General Counsel (“Senior Vice Chancellor”). Essential Functions Executive Support and Strategic Coordination Manage the Senior Vice Chancellors complex and dynamic calendar, anticipating and resolving conflicts and complications based on the Senior Vice Chancellor’s schedule and priorities. Prepare background materials, agendas, and presentations for meetings. Coordinate travel, expenses, and logistics. Monitor deadlines and follow-up actions to support the effective and efficient work of the Senior Vice Chancellor. Handle detailed and confidential information with discretion, accuracy, and timeliness. Office Operations Management Serve as a trusted administrative partner to the Senior Vice Chancellor in identifying operational priorities, implementing strategic initiatives, and supporting continuous improvement efforts. Assist with new matter intake, including tracking of attorney assignment and preparing new legal files. Manage new vendor setup, invoice tracking and payment processing, and contract renewal deadlines. Coordinate office communications, maintain departmental informational resources, and support dissemination of updates and communications to internal stakeholders. In close consultation with University Financial Services, assist with budget monitoring, expenditure tracking, financial reporting, and preparation of budget-related materials. Oversee day-to-day office operations, including ordering supplies and maintaining office records. Coordinate operational activities among OGC and partner offices including Human Resources, Civil Rights and Equal Opportunity, Enterprise Risk Management, Business and Financial Administration, Facilities, Information Technology, the Chancellors Office, and other University units. Provide notary services to support the operations of the University. Administrative Support and Communication Provide exemplary customer service as the first point of contact for internal and external constituents who interact with OGC. Monitor and answer departmental phone calls and emails, communicating accurately and professionally. Provide administrative support to all OGC attorneys, including meeting scheduling and setup; formatting and proofreading documents; copying, scanning, and filing documents; and preparing documents from templates. Assist attorneys with collection and production of documents in response to subpoenas and discovery requests. Coordinate with IT on implementation of record retention requests, litigation holds, and record collection. Support records management by maintaining and organizing files in the office’s legal file management system. Timely prepare for appropriate approval purchasing card and travel expenses for all OGC attorneys. Maintain office tracking systems and prepare administrative reports regarding office activities, service requests, and operational performance. Project Management and Process Improvement Coordinate office projects and initiatives. Track timelines, deadlines, and deliverables. Support implementation of new systems and technologies. Office Engagement, Events, and Administrative Programs Coordinate new employee and intern onboarding and training. In consultation with the Senior Vice Chancellor, plan and facilitate office team building events. Support employee engagement and professional development. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities • Exceptional organizational skills. • Strong written and verbal communication skills. • Exceptional judgment, discretion, and confidentiality. • Ability to effectively communicate with a broad range of constituencies and maintain a positive reputation for the University and OGC. • Proficient in Microsoft Outlook, Word, Excel, Adobe Acrobat, PowerPoint, Teams and Office365. Ability and willingness to learn new software, systems and processes. Required Qualifications • Bachelors degree or equivalent experience. • Two (2) years of executive support, project management, office management, or operations experience. • Experience handling confidential matters. Preferred Qualifications • Experience working in a higher education or legal setting. • Experience supporting executive leadership. • Notary Public certification or ability to obtain certification. Working Environment • Standard office environment. • Quiet-to-moderate noise. • Ability to sit in front of a computer for an extended period of time. • Occasionally required to move about the campus, with the capability of lifting up to 20 pounds. Physical Activities • Ability to work in front of a computer for extended periods of time. • Occasionally required to move about the office/campus. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. (MST) November 9, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Salary Grade Number: The salary grade for the position is 11. Salary Range: The salary range for this position is $67,000 - $78,000 The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers excellent benefits , including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, tuition benefit and ECO pass. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Please include the following documents with your application: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 457f3661 Last Name (required) 5734321a Email (required) 5387d891 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in assembly facility environment. Skilled Trade Assistant Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Skilled individual who installs, maintains and repairs all types of equipment on the DU campus including HVAC, electrical and plumbing systems; in residential houses , dormitory, academic and research facilities. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 76706d21 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list o