      "title": "Part Time Event Manager",
      "description": "Part Time Event Manager - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Part Time Event Manager 499120 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Part-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary The University of Denver's Conference & Event Services (CES) department provides event planning, coordination, and operational support for conferences, meetings, camps, and special events hosted on campus. CES partners with university departments and external organizations to deliver high-quality events that support the University's mission, strengthen community relationships, and generate revenue. The Event Manager is responsible for planning, coordinating, and executing a variety of events for external clients, faculty, staff, and campus visitors. Reporting to the Assistant Director of Event Operations, this position manages event logistics, client relationships, venue scheduling, and coordination with campus service providers to ensure successful event experiences. The ideal candidate demonstrates strong organizational, customer service, and problem-solving skills, with the ability to manage multiple priorities, build collaborative relationships, and adapt to changing event needs. This is a non-benefited position not to exceed 1,000 hours in a calendar year. Essential Functions Plan, coordinate, and execute a variety of events, including conferences, meetings, receptions, graduations, and other campus activities. Serve as a primary point of contact for clients throughout the event planning process, including conducting site tours, identifying event requirements, and providing ongoing communication and support. Manage event bookings, venue scheduling, contracts, and payment collection using event management systems, including Momentus (EBMS) and 25Live. Coordinate event logistics, including room assignments and setups, audiovisual services, catering, signage, parking, security, custodial services, and other operational needs. Manage event space assignments to maximize effective use of university facilities while coordinating with other scheduled campus activities. Collaborate with university departments, campus service providers, and external vendors to ensure event requirements are communicated and executed effectively. Provide on-site event oversight, including coordinating the work of service providers, operational staff, contractors, and student employees as needed. Monitor event activities, troubleshoot issues, and respond to changing client or operational needs to ensure successful event delivery. Support conference operations and departmental administrative activities, including event documentation, coordination with service providers, and regular communication with the Assistant Director of Event Operations. Perform additional duties as assigned to support departmental operations and events. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong organizational and project management skills, with the ability to manage multiple events, priorities, and deadlines. Excellent written and verbal communication skills, including the ability to interact professionally with diverse clients, colleagues, and stakeholders. Strong customer service skills and the ability to build positive, collaborative relationships. Ability to exercise independent judgment, demonstrate initiative, and resolve problems effectively. Strong attention to detail and commitment to delivering high-quality events and services. Ability to work effectively both independently and as part of a team in a fast-paced environment. Flexibility and adaptability to changing schedules, client needs, and operational priorities. Ability to identify opportunities to enhance client experiences and support departmental business objectives. Proficiency in Microsoft Office Suite and ability to learn event management and scheduling software. Demonstrated professionalism, dependability, and accountability. Required Qualifications Bachelor's degree or equivalent combination of education and experience. One (1) to two (2) years of related event planning, coordination, or management experience. Preferred Qualifications Three (3) or more years of event management experience in an academic setting. Certified Event Planner credential or equivalent professional certification. Experience using Momentus (EBMS) event management software. Experience using 25Live scheduling software. Experience working in higher education. Experience coordinating events involving VIP clients, high-profile guests, or donors. Working Environment Combination of standard office and active event environments across university facilities. On-site presence required to support event planning, operations, and venue oversight. Event environments may involve elevated noise levels, large groups, and fast-paced activity. Hybrid work arrangements may be available based on departmental and operational needs. Evening and weekend work may be required, particularly during peak event periods and the summer conference season. Participation in an on-call rotation may be required. Physical Activities Ability to sit and work at a computer for extended periods. Ability to stand, walk, and move between event locations across campus. Ability to lift, carry, or transport materials and equipment weighing up to 50 pounds. Work Schedule This part-time position is expected to work approximately 20 hours per week, with specific days and hours varying based on event schedules and departmental needs. Evening and weekend availability is required as needed to support events, particularly during peak conference periods. Hourly Rate: The hourly rate for the position is $25.00. The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers some benefits for non-benefited employees. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. November 6, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Please include the following documents with your application: Resume Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non-Discrimination Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 16af7a94 Last Name (required) fb1cbda9 Email (required) 1142e64c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in assembly facility environment. Skilled Trade Assistant Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Skilled individual who installs, maintains and repairs all types of equipment on the DU campus including HVAC, electrical and plumbing systems; in residential houses , dormitory, academic and research facilities. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 081387e1 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Events Events Employment Type Staff Part-Time Staff Part-Time Locations Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Denver, CO, Colorado, United States First Name (required) b3991695 Last Name (required) 1f754e85 Email (required) 5af3e856 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Copyright© 2026 University of Denver. | All rights reserved. | The University of Denver is an equal opportunity institution Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept e