    "https://jobs.du.edu/jobs/payroll-specialist-denver-co-colorado-united-states-4f7a9a93-aec7-4e9e-b909-5e68dcb6e8be": {
      "title": "Payroll Specialist",
      "description": "Payroll Specialist - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Payroll Specialist 499101 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Full-Time Closing on: Nov 2 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Payroll Department is part of the University Financial Services division at the University of Denver. The department provides high-quality payroll and tax compliance services for the University’s approximately 4,000 employees, delivered accurately, efficiently, and in compliance with federal, state, and local requirements. Position Summary Reporting to the Payroll Manager, the Payroll Specialist is responsible for the processing and timely delivery of the University’s bi-weekly payroll, including processing off-cycle payroll requests as needed. The Payroll Specialist uses an understanding of the University’s ERP and time keeping system to accurately pay employees in compliance with federal and state laws and regulations, such as the IRS and FLSA rules and regulations. The Payroll Specialist helps to assure proper tax treatment, accounting, and disposition of withholdings such as taxes, deductions for benefits, charitable contributions, retirement contributions, etc. The Payroll Specialist follows established procedures and guidelines to process payroll accurately and in compliance with university policy and applicable regulations. Essential Functions In addition to following the University of Denver’s policies and procedures, principal responsibilities include, but are not limited to: Processes the University’s bi-weekly payroll in accordance with established procedures, ensuring proper payment of wages and salaries by using the ERP and time keeping system to correctly process salaries and reported hours worked, correctly utilize paid leave and holiday pay, correctly accrue compensatory time, and correctly compute overtime while meeting deadlines. Processes off-cycle payroll requests as needed, following standard procedures to ensure accurate and timely payment outside the standard bi-weekly cycle. Ensures accurate tax withholding and treatment for employees processed through bi-weekly payroll cycles, in accordance with applicable federal, state, and local requirements. Generates and maintains supporting documentation for all payrolls. Provides support related to regulatory issues, such as non-resident aliens, social security, moving expenses, and other fringe benefits, escalating complex or non-standard situations as needed. Coordinates with Human Resources for proper benefit and deduction set-up, verifies and processes unused vacation and sick leave payouts, and terminates all payroll deductions for retiring and terminating employees. Calculates adjustments for a variety of pay rules following established guidelines. Supports the accurate issuance of W2s. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Strong analytical and problem-solving skills, with the ability to identify routine payroll issues and escalate complex or non-standard situations appropriately. Excellent written and verbal communication skills. Proficiency using payroll software in a complex environment. Ability to meet tight deadlines on a regular basis, following established procedures and guidelines. Knowledge of federal and state regulations related to employment and/or payroll practices. Trustworthiness and complete dependability in handling sensitive and confidential information. Required Qualifications Two to five (2-5) years of full-time work experience in payroll Preferred Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in a related discipline, such as finance, accounting, business administration or similar Experience using UKG Workforce Management Pro and/or Banner Payroll Experience processing bi-weekly payroll in multiple jurisdictions Fundamental Payroll Certification (FPC) by the American Payroll Association Working Environment • Standard office environment. • Unexpected interruptions occur often and stress level is moderate to high. • Noise level is quiet to moderate. Physical Activities • Ability to work in front of a computer for extended periods of time. • Occasionally required to move about the office/campus. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m.  In accordance with the University's flexible work policy, this position is eligible to be considered for partial remote work. Further details regarding this arrangement will be determined with the hiring manager and are dependent on division and team-specific needs. Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. (MST) November 2, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Salary Grade Number: The salary grade for the position is 11. Salary Range: The salary range for this position is $65,000 - $72,000. The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers excellent benefits , including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, tuition benefit and ECO pass. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Please include the following documents with your application: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) d0c42f90 Last Name (required) f4dc19a2 Email (required) dd79051c Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in assembly facility environment. Skilled Trade Assistant Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Skilled individual who installs, maintains and repairs all types of equipment on the DU campus including HVAC, electrical and plumbing systems; in residential houses , dormitory, academic and research facilities. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert f7fdae88 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Accounting / Finance Admin / Executive / Office Support Business Operations / Services Accounting / Finance Admin / Executive / Office Support Business Operations / Services Employment Type Staff Full-Time Staff Full-Time Locations Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Denver, CO, Colorado, United States First Name (required) 023458a0 Last Name (required) 7d866b58 Email (required) b98814d4 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Copyright© 2026 University of Denver. | All rights reserved. | The University of Denver is an equal opportunity institution Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you the most relevant job opportunities. With the decision \"Accept essential only\" we will respect your privacy and will not set cookies that aren't necessary for the operation of the site. Accept essential only Accept all Please choose the location(s)"
