    "https://jobs.du.edu/jobs/administrative-assistant-enrollment-denver-co-colorado-united-states-b36045b0-9680-4ff9-b754-9b28c749a7b4": {
      "title": "Administrative Assistant, Enrollment",
      "description": "Administrative Assistant, Enrollment - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Administrative Assistant, Enrollment 499100 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Full-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Enrollment Division at the University of Denver, which consists of Undergraduate Admission and Financial Aid, seeks to attract and enroll students who will become leaders, scholars, artists, entrepreneurs, and public servants uniquely qualified to live in and shape a global society. The Undergraduate Admission team recognizes education as a means of individual and societal transformation - our vision is to inspire, guide, and support prospective and current students as leaders and scholars who will positively impact their communities. In our daily work, the enrollment team is guided by these values: intentional and informed decisions; integrity and inclusion; collaboration; fiscal responsibility; spirit; clear and thoughtful communication; and exceptional quality service. The Financial Aid Office is dedicated to serving and educating students, families, colleagues, and the community through the financial aid process from pre-enrollment to program completion. We value empathy and integrity, knowledgeable and professional staff, advocacy and access, clear and consistent communication, and compliance. We have primary responsibility for the undergraduate financial aid process, and we also serve the graduate student population. Position Summary The Administrative Assistant reports to the vice chancellor for enrollment. This position is responsible for overseeing, administering, and managing the day-to-day administrative and business operations of the Enrollment Division. Essential Functions Executive and Departmental Support Assist the vice chancellor with calendar management, and assistance with scheduling larger group meetings. Help schedule events by reserving spaces, preparing materials, coordinating other executive schedules, and ordering catering and AV. Provide new employee onboarding support, as needed Expense and Timecard Approval Manage expense reports for the vice chancellor Approve monthly timecards for vice chancellor’s direct reports Recurring Transaction and Supply Administrator Oversee recurring transactions for water delivery and shredding services, ensure the division is billed correctly; coordinate these services. Order supplies Order business cards and name tags as needed Transaction Processing Coordinate with Enrollment Budget office to process various partner reimbursements for case study travel or sponsored events Coordinate with Enrollment Budget office to create invoices and process checks received for annual counselor events Request student application fee refunds from Common App when needed Submit vendor invoices to Enrollment Budget office for payment Vendor and Partnership Contract Tracking Request new vendor set-ups from the Enrollment Budget office when needed for new vendor relationships Submit and manage vendor and partnership contracts to the Enrollment Budget team Maintain Contract Tracker and PO Master and Aging spreadsheets to maintain complete records Office Management Manages office functions and act as key liaison with Facilities Management; ensure offices are complete with supplies and in working order; liaise with each department to maintain effective and efficient operations Technology and Hardware Assistance Purchase computer peripherals as needed Follow and complete acquisition and recycle computer processes with the Enrollment Budget Office Human Resources Transaction Support Coordinate the administration of employee hire/termination with the Enrollment Budget team Update the division’s organizational charts, as needed Provide administrative support to the vice chancellor for search committees Problem Solving and Reporting Identify, recognize, and resolve problems that have established precedents Compile, organize, and analyze financial information and other data Recognize, define, and resolve unique problems using operating procedures and established precedents. Other duties, as assigned Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities The ideal candidate will possess: An ability to communicate effectively with excellent written, verbal and speaking skills to connect with all audiences. Experience with Microsoft Office applications including Outlook, Teams, OneNote, Word and Excel Willingness to learn new systems and applications, as required Mathematical skillset; deductive reasoning and data analysis Keen attention to detail Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities Empathy and understanding: the ability to put yourself in your customers’ shoes and actively listen to their needs Patience and professionalism: the ability to maintain a calm and positive demeanor Ability to work with university community members and respond to their needs Ability to review, examine, and prepare documents or reports Identify, recognize, and resolve problems that have established precedents Review information for completeness and accuracy using existing guidelines Exceptionally self-motivated and directed Required Qualifications High school diploma One to two (1-2) years of relevant experience Equivalent combination of education and experience is acceptable Preferred Qualifications Higher education work experience Working Environment • Standard office environment. • Unexpected interruptions occur often and stress level is moderate to high. • Noise level is quiet to moderate. Physical Activities • Ability to work in front of a computer for extended periods of time. • Occasionally required to move about the office/campus. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. (MST) November 6, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Salary Grade Number: The salary grade for the position is 7. Hourly Range: The hourly range for the position is $24.00 - $26.00. The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers excellent benefits , including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, tuition benefit and ECO pass. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Please include the following documents with your application: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) 3fe65bc2 Last Name (required) 4dd1a960 Email (required) 284dee8f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in assembly facility environment. Skilled Trade Assistant Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Skilled individual who installs, maintains and repairs all types of equipment on the DU campus including HVAC, electrical and plumbing systems; in residential houses , dormitory, academic and research facilities. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 3e468d9c Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Admin / Executive / Office Support Customer Service Enrollment Admin / Executive / Office Support Customer Service Enrollment Employment Type Staff Full-Time Staff Full-Time Locations Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Denver, CO, Colorado, United States First Name (required) af14050a Last Name (required) 9c298f80 Email (required) 8528cc58 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Copyright© 2026 Un