    "https://jobs.du.edu/jobs/director-finance-and-operations-denver-co-colorado-united-states-a094c53b-aa54-478c-8821-7d2b0f8c1fbd": {
      "title": "Director, Finance and Operations",
      "description": "Director, Finance and Operations - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Director, Finance and Operations 499091 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Full-Time Closing on: Nov 6 2026 Add to favorites View favorites The Business Operations & Analysis Office is comprised of a team of business officers who are highly trained and efficient in University business functions. Our primary role is to support the mission of the Business and Financial Affairs (BFA) division by enabling effective financial management and operational excellence across the University of Denver. By partnering with campus stakeholders, BOA helps ensure that resources, processes, and services align with BFA’s commitment to fostering a high-performing environment for people, facilities, and infrastructure. Through this work, the team contributes directly to sustaining a strong, efficient, and well-managed university ecosystem. Position Summary The Director of Finance and Operations reports to the Business Operations and Analysis leadership team and provides leadership and oversight for financial management, human resources, and operational finance functions across the assigned units. This role is responsible for leading a team that serves academic and administrative units, including a manager(s) and multiple business officers, ensuring all financial and HR transactions are processed accurately and in a timely manner. The Director is the primary knowledge expert for their unit’s budgets and financial forecasting/budgeting. Essential Functions Lead and manage a cross-functional team responsible for executing financial, payroll, and HR transactions, ensuring high performance, accountability, and a culture of excellence and continuous improvement. Ensure operational accuracy and compliance by maintaining high standards for transaction timeliness, financial integrity, and adherence to university policies, regulatory requirements, and audit standards. Oversee financial planning and performance by developing, monitoring, and adjusting budgets and forecasts for assigned units to support informed decision-making and fiscal responsibility. Serve as the subject matter expert on financial operations, providing leadership with detailed insights into budget status, tuition and discount management (as applicable), and overall financial health. Partner with leadership on budget development and resource allocation, delivering data-driven analysis and ensure budgets align with institutional strategy and remain compliant throughout the fiscal year. Maintain audit readiness and operational integrity by preparing documentation, supporting audits and reviews, and proactively resolving financial or compliance issues. Collaborate closely with leadership to foster a high-performing team environment and cultivate a culture of excellence, accountability, and continuous improvement Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Expertise in financial management and budgeting, forecasting, and analysis for large, complex budgets to align with institutional priorities. Knowledge of HR and payroll processes, policies, and compliance standards Proficiency with ERP and financial systems (e.g., Banner, Salesforce, PeopleSoft) and reporting tools Leadership and team management skills for multi-layered and cross-functional operational teams Advanced data analysis and reporting skills using Microsoft Excel and Microsoft 365 Strong communication and collaboration skills for partnering with leadership and cross-functional teams Ability to quickly resolve operational and compliance issues and make sound decisions in complex environments Required Qualifications Bachelor’s degree in Business, Finance, Accounting, or related field Ability to work on campus 4 days a week (one remote) in an open office concept Minimum 4-7 years of progressively responsible experience in financial and administrative leadership roles. Demonstrated experience managing budgets and supervising multi-layered teams. Preferred Qualifications Advanced degree/certification (MBA, MPA, CPA or similar). Over 8 years of progressive financial leadership with increasing responsibility for team management Experience in higher education or similarly complex organizations. Familiarity with Banner, Salesforce, PeopleSoft, or similar ERP systems. Working Environment Standard office environment. Unexpected interruptions occur often and stress level is moderate to high. Noise level is quiet to moderate. Physical Activities Ability to work in front of a computer for extended periods of time. Occasionally required to move about the office/campus. Work Schedule Monday - Friday, 8:00 a.m. - 4:30 p.m. The University's working hours are 8:00am-4:30pm, Monday-Friday. This position would be eligible for one work from home day per week (Wednesday). Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. (MST) November 6, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Salary Grade Number: The salary grade for the position is 14. Salary Range: The salary range for this position is $105,000 - $115,000. The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers excellent benefits , including medical, dental, retirement, paid time off, tuition benefit and ECO pass. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Please include the following documents with your application: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) e44414f2 Last Name (required) 25980f4e Email (required) b3bc6d0f Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in a