onditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are contingent upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) cb185151 Last Name (required) ae18c295 Email (required) c0a685c9 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and the general direction of the Operations Manager of Auxiliary Facilities this position will be responsible for the performance of skilled labor tasks associated with the successful production of events and conversions in assembly facility environment. Skilled Trade Assistant Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Skilled individual who installs, maintains and repairs all types of equipment on the DU campus including HVAC, electrical and plumbing systems; in residential houses , dormitory, academic and research facilities. Sign up for job alerts Job Alert 083b5da8 Finalize your job alert by selecting criteria from the dropdowns below. You can select multiple options from each dropdown by returning to the combobox and re-entering the list of options. Submit at the end to create your job alert. Categories Faculty Faculty Employment Type Adjunct Faculty Adjunct Faculty Locations Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Denver, CO, Colorado, United States First Name (required) c8822ca9 Last Name (required) 3a87c556 Email (required) 1b6e8003 Send Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Facebook X LinkedIn Instagram Youtube Copyright© 2026 University of Denver. | All rights reserved. | The University of Denver is an equal opportunity institution Cookie Preferences Privacy Policy Candidate Details We use cookies Some are necessary to operate the website and its functions. Others help personalise, improve content and services to show you