    "https://jobs.du.edu/jobs/ritchie-center-event-operations-associate-denver-co-colorado-united-states": {
      "title": "Ritchie Center Event Operations Associate",
      "description": "Ritchie Center Event Operations Associate - Denver, CO, Colorado, United States Jobs@DU Benefits Compensation Community Support and Engagement Need Help? My Profile Kiosk mode Your Work Matters Here. At DU, every role contributes to a community where students and employees can grow, connect, find purpose, and thrive. In compliance with the Americans with Disabilities Act (ADA), the Rehabilitation Act of 1973, and University of Denver policy, DU provides reasonable accommodations to provide equal access to job opportunities, job performance, and workplace benefits. Visit DU Accessibility to learn more about reasonable accommodations and accessibility. To request reasonable accommodations please contact the ADA Coordinator in The Office of Civil Rights & Equal Opportunity (CREO) at ADA.Coordinator@du.edu or by calling 303-871-3941. Ritchie Center Event Operations Associate 498981 Denver, CO, Colorado Staff Part-Time Add to favorites View favorites Position Summary Event Operation Associates are responsible for assisting with a variety of event day operations at the Daniel L. Ritchie Center for Sports & Wellness. Associates will assist in the game operations of DU Varsity Sports, including hockey, gymnastics, volleyball, basketball, soccer, and lacrosse. Additionally, they will contribute to the successful delivery of a variety of other events, such as expos, banquets, special ceremonies, and more. This is a non-benefited position not to exceed 1,000 hours in a calendar year. Essential Functions Support the division of Athletics and Recreation with its execution of Ritchie Center event operations. Assist in the game operations and game day production for varsity athletics. Serve as a guest services member during Ritchie Center events. Knowledge, Skills, and Abilities Provide excellent customer service for all Ritchie Center participants and customers. Recognize and respond effectively and efficiently to emergencies. Maintain a clean and safe environment. Able to work both individually and as part of a team. Communicate clearly and effectively to participants, customers, and coworkers. Required Qualifications Current DU undergraduate or graduate student enrolled for the 2026-2027 academic year, or recent college graduate with a related degree. Work evenings, nights, weekends, and other non-traditional hours. Preferred Qualifications Previous experience working in event operations, sports management, or customer service. Knowledge of NCAA athletics and familiarity with sports such as hockey, gymnastics, volleyball, basketball, soccer, and lacrosse. Strong interpersonal and communication skills with the ability to work effectively in a team environment. Ability to stay organized, multitask, and remain calm in fast-paced or high-pressure situations. Demonstrated reliability, punctuality, and a strong work ethic. Comfortable using basic technology (e.g., radios, ticketing scanners, scoreboards, or basic A/V equipment). CPR/First Aid certification (preferred but not required). Availability to work evenings, weekends, and holidays based on event schedules. Work Schedule Varies Physical Activities Be able to stand for long periods of time. Be able to lift 20 pounds. Working Environment This role requires a flexible schedule, including frequent evening and weekend shifts, based on event demands. Work is primarily conducted on-site at the Daniel L. Ritchie Center for Sports & Wellness and its surrounding facilities. Physical activity is required, including standing for extended periods, walking long distances, lifting up to 20 lbs, and assisting with event set-up and tear-down. Fast-paced, dynamic environment with exposure to large crowds, loud noise levels, and various weather conditions for outdoor events. Collaborative, team-oriented workplace with a strong focus on providing a positive and safe experience for all event attendees and participants. Hourly Rate: The hourly rate for the position is $19.29. The University of Denver has provided a compensation range that represents its good faith estimate of what the University may pay for the position at the time of posting. The University may ultimately pay more or less than the posted compensation range. The salary offered to the selected candidate will be determined based on factors such as the qualifications of the selected candidate, departmental budget availability, internal salary equity considerations, and available market information, but not based on a candidate’s sex or any other protected status. Benefits: The University of Denver offers some benefits for non-benefited employees. The University of Denver is a private institution that empowers students who want to make a difference. Learn more about the University of Denver . Application Deadline For consideration, please submit your application materials by 4:00 p.m. (MST) October 19, 2026. Special Instructions Candidates must apply online through jobs.du.edu to be considered. Only applications submitted online will be accepted. Please include the following documents with your application: 1. Resume 2. Cover Letter The University of Denver is an equal opportunity employer. All qualified applicants will receive consideration for employment without regard to race, color, religion, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital, family, or parental status, pregnancy or related conditions, national origin, disability, or status as a protected veteran. The University of Denver does not discriminate and prohibits discrimination on the basis of race, color, national origin, ancestry, age, religion, creed, disability, sex (including sex stereotypes, sex characteristics, sexual orientation, gender identity, and gender expression), marital family, and parental status, pregnancy, genetic information, military enlistment, or veteran status, and any other class of individuals protected from discrimination under federal, state, or local law, regulation, or ordinance in any of the University’s educational programs and activities, and in the employment (including application for employment) and admissions (including application for admission) context, as required by Title IX of the Education Amendments of 1972; the Americans with Disabilities Act; Section 504 of the Rehabilitation Act of 1973; Title VI and VII of the Civil Rights Act of 1964; the Age Discrimination Act of 1975; the Age Discrimination in Employment Act of 1967; the Equal Pay Act; the Colorado Equal Pay for Equal Work Act; the Colorado Protecting Opportunities and Worker's Rights (\"POWR\") Act; and any other federal, state, and local laws, regulations, or ordinances that prohibit discrimination, harassment, and/or retaliation. For more information, please see the University of Denver's Non‑Discrimination‑Statement . All offers of employment are based upon satisfactory completion of a criminal history and National Sex Offender Registry background check. Back to job search Apply Now First Name (required) ff2bd52f Last Name (required) 34abe08f Email (required) c1472075 Refer someone to this job Apply Please wait... Done Not You? Thank you Recommended Jobs Research Lab Coordinator, Department of Psychology Denver, CO, Colorado Lab Administration/Management, Research The Research Lab Coordinator will play a central role in launching and managing the Self-Regulation, Adaptation, and Growing Experiences (SAGE) Lab at the University of Denver, directed by Dr. Meriah DeJoseph.  Primary responsibilities include assisting with study development and protocol implementation, managing IRB submissions, recruiting and scheduling participants, coordinating data collection, overseeing research assistants, and managing and cleaning data. Building Services Specialist Denver, CO, Colorado Facilities Management & Planning, Maintenance / Grounds / Skilled Trades Under the general direct supervision of the Conversion Manager and